.TH FL-CLOCK 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.4" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-clock \- world clocks, alarms, a timer and a stopwatch
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-clock\fR [\fB\-\-page\fR world|alarms|timer|stopwatch]
.br
\fBfl-clock \-\-alarms\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBWorld Clocks\fR shows the time here and in the cities you add, with
their difference to the local time. \fBAlarms\fR ring at a time once or on
chosen days of the week: a notification with Snooze (10 minutes) and Stop,
and a sound. \fBTimer\fR counts down a duration (5, 1:30, 1h30m) and
\fBStopwatch\fR counts up, with laps.
.PP
Alarms ring while Clock is open. With "Ring alarms when Clock is closed",
\fBfl-clock \-\-alarms\fR (no window) rings them; it starts with the session
(\fI~/.config/autostart/fl-clock-alarms.desktop\fR).
.SH FILES
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/clock.ini\fR: the cities and the alarms.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-notifyd\fR(1)
